{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 15:46:22 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 22:46:22 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nThe reassembly bound uses accumulated chunk bytes and checks the completed payload’s actual length; the near-limit regression covers delivery of a valid message ([udp.cljc:339](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc:339), [udp_test.cljc:127](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/udp_test.cljc:127)). The JVM receiver resets the packet length before every receive, with a loopback regression for a short datagram followed by a longer one ([jvm.clj:30](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/clj/dao/stream/udp/jvm.clj:30), [jvm_test.clj:24](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/udp/jvm_test.clj:24)). The direction values accepted by validation match those emitted by the sender. A zero-length chunk passes the host byte-type check, so validation does not reject it on length alone ([udp.cljc:143](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc:143), [udp.cljc:273](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc:273)).\n\n**Remaining P2:** Fragment recognition requires `:dao.stream.udp/part`. A fragment-shaped datagram with `:parts`, `:direction`, and `:bytes` but a missing `:part` bypasses validation and is deposited as an ordinary value. That violates the claimed malformed-fragment drop behavior ([udp.cljc:268](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc:268), [udp.cljc:383](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc:383)). The seven malformed test shapes do not cover a missing `:part` ([udp_test.cljc:170](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/udp_test.cljc:170)).\n\nI could not rerun the focused tests: the read-only environment prevented Clojure from creating its classpath cache. No files were edited.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
